{% set local_problem %}
<p>We've watched Hartselle grow over the past 20+ years. The historic homes downtown — many with original sectional gutters — need updates that respect their character while providing modern protection. The newer developments spreading across Morgan County need gutters that can handle the area's demanding rainfall and soil conditions.</p>

<p>Hartselle's agricultural heritage means different drainage patterns than urban areas. Open land, farm properties, and the varied terrain throughout Morgan County create unique challenges. Water behaves differently here than in dense subdivisions, and gutter systems need to account for that.</p>

<p>Traditional sectional gutters — the kind with seams every 10 feet — struggle in our climate. Each seam is a potential leak point that weakens over time. During heavy storms, water finds these weak spots and starts causing damage to fascia, siding, and foundations.</p>

<p>Seamless gutters eliminate these problems. Custom-fabricated on-site to fit your home exactly, they have no seams to fail. For Hartselle homes — whether historic or new — seamless gutters provide the reliable protection our weather demands.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Seamless gutters are exactly what they sound like: continuous gutters with no seams except at corners and downspout connections. Unlike traditional sectional gutters (made of pre-cut 10-foot sections joined together), seamless gutters are fabricated on-site from a single piece of aluminum coil — custom-cut to the exact length of each run on your home.</p>

<p>Why does this matter? Because seams are where gutters fail. Every joint in a sectional gutter system is a potential leak point, a place for debris to catch, and a weak spot that can separate over time. Seamless gutters eliminate these problems entirely.</p>

<p>We bring our portable gutter machine directly to your Hartselle home, feed in aluminum coil, and fabricate your gutters right in your driveway. What comes out is a precision-fit gutter system designed specifically for your roofline — not generic sections forced to fit.</p>
{% endset %}

